# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DOCKER BUILD CONTEXT FILTER
#
# This file is the single biggest lever on Railway deploy time. Before it was
# expanded, the context was ~6 GB (asset kits, image corpora, archives, zips)
# and every deploy re-uploaded all of it before Docker even started.
#
# MATCHING RULES (moby/patternmatcher — same engine BuildKit uses):
#   • A leading "/" is stripped when the file is parsed, so "/docs" == "docs".
#     We write the slash anyway to DOCUMENT that the pattern is root-anchored.
#   • "*" does NOT cross "/". So "*.md" matches ONLY root-level .md files —
#     it does NOT match lib/story/coach/knowledge/*.md. Use "**/" for any-depth.
#   • Last matching line wins, so "!" exceptions must come after the exclusion.
#
# 🚨 THINGS THAT MUST NEVER BE EXCLUDED (verified by grepping the source):
#   public/          — 3.8 GB, but the Dockerfile copies it into
#                      .next/standalone; the app 404s everything without it.
#                      EXCEPTION (Aug 2026): the seven paths in the
#                      "MIGRATED TO SUPABASE STORAGE" block below. Those were
#                      audited (zero fs.*/generateStaticParams reads — every
#                      reference is a browser-side href/src/fetch), moved to
#                      the `static-assets` bucket, and are now served via
#                      next.config.ts `rewrites()` (afterFiles). They are the
#                      ONLY public/ subpaths safe to drop from the build
#                      context — do not add siblings here without the same
#                      audit.
#   data/            — lib/data.ts and lib/montree/guru/knowledge-retriever.ts
#                      read process.cwd()/data/{videos.json,guru_knowledge/…}.
#   scripts/         — app/api/whale/reports/pdf spawns
#                      process.cwd()/scripts/generate_parent_report.py.
#   *.xlsx at root   — app/api/montree/super-admin/master-outreach/download
#                      reads process.cwd()/Montree_Master_Outreach.xlsx.
#   lib/**/*.md      — runtime knowledge bases (story coach, mira, tracy,
#                      social-media-guru) are loaded by readdir/readFile.
#   assets/          — app/api/guides/language-making-guide reads it.
#   .env             — NOT excluded; next build may read it. Only *.local is.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Original exclusions (kept verbatim) ──────────────────────────────────────
node_modules
.next
.git
.env.local
.env*.local
*.md
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
*.log
coverage
.nyc_output
dist
build

# Defensive: the "*.md" line above is root-level-only by Docker's rules, but
# these markdown trees are read at RUNTIME — make it impossible to lose them.
!lib/**/*.md
!app/**/*.md
!components/**/*.md

# ── MIGRATED TO SUPABASE STORAGE (Aug 2026) ───────────────────────────────────
# These five directories + two video files were the git/public
# static-asset store for the Dark Phonics / SATPIN library and the landing
# splash film. They now live in the Supabase `static-assets` bucket
# (same subpaths) and are proxied back to their original public/ URLs by
# next.config.ts `rewrites()`, so no page/component code changed. They stay
# on disk on the dev machine (not deleted, not git-removed here) but are
# safe to drop from the Docker build context because nothing reads them off
# the filesystem — confirmed by grepping the whole app for fs.*/readFile/
# path.join(process.cwd()/generateStaticParams hits against these names
# (pre-migration audit, see MIGRATION_NOTES_static-assets.md).
/public/dark-phonics-books
/public/dark-phonics-materials
/public/satpin-books
/public/satpin-materials
/public/shelf-packs
/public/montree-splash-video.mp4
/public/montree-splash-video-zh.mp4

# ── Large asset corpora (zero references in app/ lib/ components/) ───────────
/materials-out
/phonics-images
/docs
/_video_assets
/_assets_incoming

# ── Native / Capacitor build outputs (web build is `next build` only; the
#    native path is `npm run build:native`, which is never run in this image) ─
/android
/ios
/native
/native-assets
/out

# ── Marketing + one-off asset kits (zero references) ─────────────────────────
/evaluation-kit
/montage-kit
/Montree Kit*
/Montree Marketing Kit
/resume-branding-kit
/social

# ── Sibling services, not part of this image ────────────────────────────────
/potato-worker
/montage-worker

# ── Archives, scratch dirs, incoming staging ────────────────────────────────
/archive
/_ARCHIVE
/_to_delete
/_verify
/_incoming-*
/_tmp_*

# ── Dev-only tooling and tests (not imported by the build) ──────────────────
/tests
/.github
/.githooks
/.claude
/.cursor

# ── Junk / generated files at the context root ──────────────────────────────
/*.zip
/*.tar.gz
/*.tgz
/*.patch
/*.command
/*.pdf
/tsconfig.*.tmp.json
/.tsc-*.json
/verify_seed_tmp*

# ── Python bytecode anywhere (scripts/ ships .py, never .pyc) ───────────────
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
